.SS "void * ecalloc_impl (size_t number, size_t size, const char * file, int line, const char * func)"

.PP
This function replaces calloc in code, and causes the program to exit when memory cannot be allocated rather than permit undefined behavior\&. This function replaces calloc in code, and causes the program to exit when memory cannot be allocated rather than permit undefined behavior\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fInumber\fP The number of blocks to allocate in memory 
.br
\fIsize\fP The size of each block in bytes 
.br
\fIfile\fP The filename of the function calling ecalloc 
.br
\fIline\fP The line number ecalloc was called 
.br
\fIfunc\fP The function calling ecalloc
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Pointer to a block of memory of the requested size, if it can be allocated
.RE
.PP

.SS "void efree_impl (void ** ptr, const char * file, int line, const char * func)"
